<body>
  <%- include('./partials/nav') %>
  <main class="container-fluid p-3 info-container">
    <div class="intro">
      <h1 class="text-center">Give your campaign a home</h1>
      <p>Keep session notes, maps, character sheets, and group discussions in one shared place.</p>
      <p>Invite your players into a Wyrld so everyone can find what they need before the next adventure.</p>
      <div class="seo-cta-block"><a class="seo-cta-primary" href="/register">Create a free account</a> <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/pricing">See plans</a>
        <p><small>Players need free accounts to join your Wyrld.</small></p>
      </div><hr>
    </div>
    <section id="what">
      <h2>Pick up where you left off</h2>
      <p>Keep session summaries, NPC details, lore, and handouts with the campaign.</p>
      <p>When someone needs to remember a name, revisit a discovery, or catch up on last week, there’s a place to look.</p>
      <figure class="toolshot-card">
        <img src="/assets/screen_shots/wyrld-record.png" alt="Wyrld record editor with campaign notes." loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Keep lore, NPC details, and session notes with your campaign.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section id="campaign-resources">
      <h2>Bring your maps and characters together</h2>
      <p>Create campaign tables, organize shared maps and tokens, and connect player character sheets.</p>
      <p>Your group can return to those resources across sessions as the adventure grows.</p>
      <div class="toolshot-grid toolshot-grid--three">
        <figure class="toolshot-card">
          <img src="/assets/screen_shots/library_screenshot.png" alt="Shared image library with folders and assets." loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Organize the maps and tokens your campaign uses.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="toolshot-card">
          <img src="/assets/screen_shots/character_sheet_adren.png" alt="Linked D&amp;D 5E character sheet." loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Keep player characters connected to the campaign.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="toolshot-card">
          <img src="/assets/screen_shots/vtt-screenshot.png" alt="Virtual tabletop with a campaign encounter." loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Return to your campaign’s tables each session.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="why">
      <h2>Keep the conversation going</h2>
      <p>Use campaign discussions for planning, announcements, and between-session conversation.</p>
      <p>Keep calendars and timelines alongside your notes, whether you’re tracking the world’s history or planning what comes next.</p>
      <figure class="toolshot-card">
        <img src="/assets/screen_shots/wyrld-community-discussion.png" alt="Campaign discussion board with threads and replies." loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Give your group a place to plan between sessions.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section id="dashboard">
      <h2>See what’s happening</h2>
      <p>The Wyrld overview brings recent activity, tables, records, sheets, and shared resources together.</p>
      <p>Find the part of the campaign you need and get back to preparing or playing.</p>
      <figure class="toolshot-card">
        <img src="/assets/screen_shots/wyrld-dash-overview.png" alt="Wyrld overview with recent activity and shared campaign resources." loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Find recent activity and your campaign’s resources in one place.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section id="how">
      <h2>Invite your group</h2>
      <p>Create a Wyrld, give it a name, and invite your players. Members join with free accounts and can link their character sheets.</p>
      <p>Add your campaign notes, maps, and other resources as you need them.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="roles">
      <h2>Choose who can do what</h2>
      <p>Wyrlds are private by default and built around invited members.</p>
      <p>Owners manage membership and settings. Managers can help maintain campaign resources, while members participate with the access their role allows.</p>
      <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/wyrld-permissions-guide">Read the permissions guide</a>
    </section>
    <section id="public-discovery">
      <h2>Open your doors when you’re ready</h2>
      <p>If you want to recruit, optional public discovery can help new players find your campaign.</p>
      <p>You decide whether to enable it.</p>
      <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/public-wyrlds-guide">Learn about public Wyrlds</a>
    </section>
    <section id="start">
      <h2>Make room for the next chapter</h2>
      <p>Bring your group and its adventures together.</p>
      <div class="seo-cta-block"><a class="seo-cta-primary" href="/register">Create a free account</a> <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/pricing">See plans</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <%- include('./partials/footer') %>
</body>

</html>
